#: ../../../api/generated/pygmt.Figure.text.rst:0
msgid "Parameters"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/src/text.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.src.text.text:44
msgid ""
"A file name or a list of file names containing one or more records. Each "
"record has the following columns:  * *x*: X coordinate or longitude * *y*: Y "
"coordinate or latitude * *angle*: Angle in degrees counter-clockwise from "
"horizontal * *font*: Text size, font, and color * *justify*:   :doc:`2-"
"character justification code </techref/justification_codes>` * *text*: The "
"text string to typeset  The *angle*, *font*, and *justify* columns are "
"optional and can be set by using the ``angle``, ``font``, and ``justify`` "
"parameters, respectively. If these parameters are set to ``True``, then the "
"corresponding columns must be present in the input file(s) and the columns "
"must be in the order mentioned above."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/src/text.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.src.text.text:44
msgid ""
"A file name or a list of file names containing one or more records. Each "
"record has the following columns:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/src/text.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.src.text.text:47
msgid "*x*: X coordinate or longitude"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/src/text.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.src.text.text:48
msgid "*y*: Y coordinate or latitude"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/src/text.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.src.text.text:49
msgid "*angle*: Angle in degrees counter-clockwise from horizontal"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/src/text.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.src.text.text:50
msgid "*font*: Text size, font, and color"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/src/text.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.src.text.text:51
msgid ""
"*justify*: :doc:`2-character justification code </techref/"
"justification_codes>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/src/text.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.src.text.text:53
msgid "*text*: The text string to typeset"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/src/text.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.src.text.text:55
msgid ""
"The *angle*, *font*, and *justify* columns are optional and can be set by "
"using the ``angle``, ``font``, and ``justify`` parameters, respectively. If "
"these parameters are set to ``True``, then the corresponding columns must be "
"present in the input file(s) and the columns must be in the order mentioned "
"above."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/src/text.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.src.text.text:61
msgid ""
"The x and y coordinates, or an array of x and y coordinates to plot the text."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/src/text.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.src.text.text:65
msgid ""
"Set reference point on the plot for the text by using x, y coordinates "
"extracted from ``region`` instead of providing them through ``x``/``y``. "
"Specify with a :doc:`2-character justification code </techref/"
"justification_codes>`. For example, ``position=\"TL\"`` plots the text at "
"the Top Left corner of the plot."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/src/text.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.src.text.text:72
msgid "The text string, or an array of strings to plot on the figure."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/src/text.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.src.text.text:74
msgid ""
"Set the angle measured in degrees counter-clockwise from horizontal (e.g. 30 "
"sets the text at 30 degrees). If no angle is explicitly given (i.e. "
"``angle=True``) then the input to ``textfiles`` must have this as a column."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/src/text.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.src.text.text:79
msgid ""
"Set the font specification with format *size*\\ ,\\ *font*\\ ,\\ *color* "
"where *size* is text size in points, *font* is the font to use, and *color* "
"sets the font color. For example, ``font=\"12p,Helvetica-Bold,red\"`` "
"selects a 12p, red, Helvetica-Bold font. If no font info is explicitly given "
"(i.e. ``font=True``), then the input to ``textfiles`` must have this "
"information in one of its columns."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/src/text.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.src.text.text:87
msgid ""
"Set the alignment which refers to the part of the text string that will be "
"mapped onto the (x, y) point. Choose a :doc:`2-character justification code "
"</techref/justification_codes>`, e.g., **BL** for Bottom Left. If no "
"justification is explicitly given (i.e. ``justify=True``), then the input to "
"``textfiles`` must have this as a column."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/src/text.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.src.text.text:93
msgid ""
"[*dx/dy*][**+to**\\|\\ **O**\\|\\ **c**\\|\\ **C**]. Adjust the clearance "
"between the text and the surrounding box [Default is 15% of the font size]. "
"Only used if ``pen`` or ``fill`` are specified. Append the unit you want "
"(**c** for centimeters, **i** for inches, or **p** for points; if not given "
"we consult :gmt-term:`PROJ_LENGTH_UNIT`) or *%* for a percentage of the font "
"size. Optionally, use modifier **+t** to set the shape of the text box when "
"using ``fill`` and/or ``pen``. Append lowercase **o** to get a straight "
"rectangle [Default is **o**]. Append uppercase **O** to get a rounded "
"rectangle. In paragraph mode (*paragraph*) you can also append lowercase "
"**c** to get a concave rectangle or append uppercase **C** to get a convex "
"rectangle."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/src/text.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.src.text.text:107
msgid "Set color for filling text boxes [Default is no fill]."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/src/text.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.src.text.text:109
msgid ""
"Set the pen used to draw a rectangle around the text string (see "
"``clearance``) [Default is ``\"0.25p,black,solid\"``]."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/src/text.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.src.text.text:112
msgid ""
"(*dx*, *dy*) or [**j**\\|\\ **J**]\\ *dx*\\[/*dy*][**+v**\\[*pen*]]. Offset "
"the text from the projected (x, y) point by (*dx*, *dy*) [Default is (0, "
"0)]. If *dy* is not specified then it is set equal to *dx*. Use **j** to "
"offset the text away from the point instead (i.e., the text justification "
"will determine the direction of the shift). Using **J** will shorten "
"diagonal offsets at corners by sqrt(2). Optionally, append **+v** which will "
"draw a line from the original point to the shifted point; append a pen to "
"change the attributes for this line."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/src/text.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.src.text.text:121
msgid "Do **not** clip text at the frame boundaries [Default is ``False``]."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/src/text.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.src.text.text:123
msgid ""
"*projcode*\\[*projparams*/]\\ *width*\\|\\ *scale*. Select map :doc:"
"`projection </projections/index>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/src/text.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.src.text.text:125
msgid ""
"*xmin/xmax/ymin/ymax*\\ [**+r**][**+u**\\ *unit*]. Specify the :doc:`region "
"</tutorials/basics/regions>` of interest. *Required if this is the first "
"plot command.*"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/src/text.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.src.text.text:129
msgid "Select verbosity level [:term:`Full usage <verbose>`]."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/src/text.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.src.text.text:131
msgid ""
"[*col*\\ =]\\ *name*\\ [,...]. Control how aspatial data are handled during "
"input and output. Full documentation is at :gmt-docs:`gmt.html#aspatial-"
"full`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/src/text.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.src.text.text:136
msgid ""
"Select a specific subplot panel. Only allowed when used in :meth:`Figure."
"subplot` mode.  - ``True`` to advance to the next panel in the selected "
"order. - *index* to specify the index of the desired panel. - (*row*, *col*) "
"to specify the row and column of the desired panel.  The panel order is "
"determined by the :meth:`Figure.subplot` method. *row*, *col* and *index* "
"all start at 0."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/src/text.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.src.text.text:136
msgid ""
"Select a specific subplot panel. Only allowed when used in :meth:`Figure."
"subplot` mode."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/src/text.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.src.text.text:139
msgid "``True`` to advance to the next panel in the selected order."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/src/text.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.src.text.text:140
msgid "*index* to specify the index of the desired panel."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/src/text.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.src.text.text:141
msgid "(*row*, *col*) to specify the row and column of the desired panel."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/src/text.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.src.text.text:143
msgid ""
"The panel order is determined by the :meth:`Figure.subplot` method. *row*, "
"*col* and *index* all start at 0."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/src/text.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.src.text.text:145
msgid ""
"[**~**]\\ *\"pattern\"* \\| [**~**]/\\ *regexp*/[**i**]. Only pass records "
"that match the given *pattern* or regular expressions [Default processes all "
"records]. Prepend **~** to the *pattern* or *regexp* to instead only pass "
"data expressions that do not match the pattern. Append **i** for case "
"insensitive matching. This does not apply to headers or segment headers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/src/text.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.src.text.text:152
msgid ""
"[**i**\\|\\ **o**]\\ *colinfo*. Specify data types of input and/or output "
"columns (time or geographical data). Full documentation is at :gmt-docs:`gmt."
"html#f-full`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/src/text.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.src.text.text:156
msgid ""
"[**i**\\|\\ **o**][*n*][**+c**][**+d**][**+m**\\ *segheader*][**+r** "
"*remark*][**+t**\\ *title*]. Specify that input and/or output file(s) have "
"*n* header records [Default is 0]. Prepend **i** if only the primary input "
"should have header records. Prepend **o** to control the writing of header "
"records, with the following modifiers supported:  - **+d** to remove "
"existing header records. - **+c** to add a header comment with column names "
"to the   output [Default is no column names]. - **+m** to add a segment "
"header *segheader* to the output   after the header block [Default is no "
"segment header]. - **+r** to add a *remark* comment to the output [Default "
"is no   comment]. The *remark* string may contain \\\\n to indicate   line-"
"breaks. - **+t** to add a *title* comment to the output [Default is no   "
"title]. The *title* string may contain \\\\n to indicate   line-breaks.  "
"Blank lines and lines starting with \\# are always skipped."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/src/text.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.src.text.text:156
msgid ""
"[**i**\\|\\ **o**][*n*][**+c**][**+d**][**+m**\\ *segheader*][**+r** "
"*remark*][**+t**\\ *title*]. Specify that input and/or output file(s) have "
"*n* header records [Default is 0]. Prepend **i** if only the primary input "
"should have header records. Prepend **o** to control the writing of header "
"records, with the following modifiers supported:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/src/text.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.src.text.text:163
msgid "**+d** to remove existing header records."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/src/text.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.src.text.text:164
msgid ""
"**+c** to add a header comment with column names to the output [Default is "
"no column names]."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/src/text.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.src.text.text:166
msgid ""
"**+m** to add a segment header *segheader* to the output after the header "
"block [Default is no segment header]."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/src/text.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.src.text.text:168
msgid ""
"**+r** to add a *remark* comment to the output [Default is no comment]. The "
"*remark* string may contain \\\\n to indicate line-breaks."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/src/text.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.src.text.text:171
msgid ""
"**+t** to add a *title* comment to the output [Default is no title]. The "
"*title* string may contain \\\\n to indicate line-breaks."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/src/text.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.src.text.text:175
msgid "Blank lines and lines starting with \\# are always skipped."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/src/text.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.src.text.text:177
msgid ""
"Select a specific word from the trailing text, with the first word being 0 "
"[Default is the entire trailing text]. No numerical columns can be specified."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/src/text.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.src.text.text:182
msgid ""
"Select perspective view and set the azimuth and elevation of the viewpoint.  "
"Accepts a single value or a sequence of two or three values: *azimuth*, "
"(*azimuth*, *elevation*), or (*azimuth*, *elevation*, *zlevel*).  - "
"*azimuth*: Azimuth angle of the viewpoint in degrees [Default is 180,   i."
"e., looking from south to north]. - *elevation*: Elevation angle of the "
"viewpoint above the horizon [Default   is 90, i.e., looking straight down at "
"nadir]. - *zlevel*: Z-level at which 2-D elements (e.g., the plot frame) are "
"drawn.   Only applied when used together with ``zsize`` or ``zscale``. "
"[Default is   at the bottom of the z-axis].  Alternatively, set "
"``perspective=True`` to reuse the perspective setting from the previous "
"plotting method, or pass a string following the full GMT syntax for finer "
"control (e.g., adding ``+w`` or ``+v`` modifiers to select an axis location "
"other than the plot origin). See :gmt-docs:`gmt.html#perspective-full` for "
"details."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/src/text.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.src.text.text:182
msgid ""
"Select perspective view and set the azimuth and elevation of the viewpoint."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/src/text.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.src.text.text:184
msgid ""
"Accepts a single value or a sequence of two or three values: *azimuth*, "
"(*azimuth*, *elevation*), or (*azimuth*, *elevation*, *zlevel*)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/src/text.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.src.text.text:187
msgid ""
"*azimuth*: Azimuth angle of the viewpoint in degrees [Default is 180, i.e., "
"looking from south to north]."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/src/text.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.src.text.text:189
msgid ""
"*elevation*: Elevation angle of the viewpoint above the horizon [Default is "
"90, i.e., looking straight down at nadir]."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/src/text.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.src.text.text:191
msgid ""
"*zlevel*: Z-level at which 2-D elements (e.g., the plot frame) are drawn. "
"Only applied when used together with ``zsize`` or ``zscale``. [Default is at "
"the bottom of the z-axis]."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/src/text.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.src.text.text:195
msgid ""
"Alternatively, set ``perspective=True`` to reuse the perspective setting "
"from the previous plotting method, or pass a string following the full GMT "
"syntax for finer control (e.g., adding ``+w`` or ``+v`` modifiers to select "
"an axis location other than the plot origin). See :gmt-docs:`gmt."
"html#perspective-full` for details."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/src/text.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.src.text.text:200
msgid ""
"Set transparency level, in [0-100] percent range [Default is ``0``, i.e., "
"opaque]. Only visible when PDF or raster format output is selected. Only the "
"PNG format selection adds a transparency layer in the image (for further "
"processing). ``transparency`` can also be a 1-D array to set varying "
"transparency for texts, but this option is only valid if using ``x``/``y`` "
"and ``text``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/src/text.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.src.text.text:208
msgid ""
"**y**\\|\\ **a**\\|\\ **w**\\|\\ **d**\\|\\ **h**\\|\\ **m**\\|\\ **s**\\| "
"**c**\\ *period*\\ [/*phase*][**+c**\\ *col*]. Convert the input *x*-"
"coordinate to a cyclical coordinate, or a different column if selected via "
"**+c**\\ *col*. The following cyclical coordinate transformations are "
"supported:  - **y**: yearly cycle (normalized) - **a**: annual cycle "
"(monthly) - **w**: weekly cycle (day) - **d**: daily cycle (hour) - **h**: "
"hourly cycle (minute) - **m**: minute cycle (second) - **s**: second cycle "
"(second) - **c**: custom cycle (normalized)  Full documentation is at :gmt-"
"docs:`gmt.html#w-full`."
msgstr ""

